      "properties": {
        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Image -> Layers -> Semantic routing\n\nDrop your picture into **Load Image**, then Queue.\n\n### How many layers do I get?\n`Empty Qwen Image Layered Latent` has a **layers** widget (set to 3 here). The decode\nreturns **layers + 1** frames, so you get 4 images out of `VAE Decode` \u2014 wired to\n**Preview: raw layers** so you can see exactly what the model produced.\n\n### You cannot ask for \"water, person, raft\" by name\nQwen's own template says the prompt \"is **not** designed to control the semantic content\nof individual layers explicitly.\" It describes the whole picture; the model chooses the\ndecomposition. That is precisely why the semantic nodes exist: you don't control WHICH\nlayer is which, so you identify them afterwards and route by meaning.\n\n### Detection is automatic\n`Semantic Layer Analyze` defaults to the **florence2** analyzer, which captions every\nlayer from its own pixels. Nothing to type, and reordering the layers reorders the\ndescriptions with them \u2014 the whole point of the semantic routing.\n\n**First run downloads ~0.5 GB of Florence-2 weights.** Slow once, fast after.\n\nSet **`composite_layer` = `first`** on `Semantic Layer Normalize`: Qwen returns the\nflattened composite as plane 0, and marking it keeps it out of the routing.\n\nSwitch the analyzer to `captions` only if you already have a captioner node in the graph\n(wire its STRING output into `captions`) or you want to override by hand.\n\n### Size\n640px is the recommended input; the latent is sized from the scaled image via\n`Get Image Size`, so it always matches. Sampling here is steps 20 / cfg 2.5; the\noriginal settings are 50 / 4.0 and roughly double the time."
      ],
      "title": "Read me first"
    },
